<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly steady.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly steady.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly steady Wednesday, grain merchandisers in the High Plains said.</p>
<p>Dealers continued to scour the country for clues that might pinpoint the extent of freeze damage to the crop. But many dealers conceded that it was still too early to tell, and they warned that the wheat's relatively healthy-looking exterior probably belied a sickly interior.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody's out checking the fields. According to the newspaper here, agronomists think Oklahoma may have suffered a 50 percent loss (in yield),&quot; a northern Oklahoma dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers reported mixed levels of movement. One Kansas dealer said farmers turned sellers early Tuesday after the board faltered, but two Oklahoma dealers said business was extremely slow Tuesday.  </p>
